2026-11-05T07:21:04.130-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="2017993f-7c67-4ca7-829e-8101163f177f" status="approved" answer="The minimist package is affected by prototype pollution via CVE-2021-44906 in versions **>= 1.0.0 and < 1.2.6** (critical severity). This vulnerability allows attackers to pollute prototypes through crafted command-line arguments. The fix was released in version 1.2.6. No other versions are impacted according to the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-03, ID 20076). This range covers all minimist versions from the initial release up to (but excluding) 1.2.6. Users must update to 1.2.6 or later to resolve the critical prototype pollution risk. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-03 (s0036_rel id 20076): minimist affected >= 1.0.0, < 1.2.6, severity critical. CVE-2021-44906: Prototype pollution through crafted command-line arguments. Fixed in 1.2.6."
