2026-11-05T07:21:48.655-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="f39f520e-b655-4122-8114-529abb9a39ad" status="approved" answer="To fix the PyYAML full_load code execution vulnerability (CVE-2020-14343), **upgrade pyyaml to \u22655.4.1** immediately. This version patch resolves the critical arbitrary code execution risk when untrusted YAML is parsed using `full_load` or `FullLoader` (as documented in VULN-0036-HW9-04). \n\nWhile upgrading is the primary fix, **always use `safe_load`** instead of `full_load` for untrusted input to prevent code execution. Additionally, **validate all input** to ensure it adheres to expected structures before parsing. This combination addresses the root cause: untrusted YAML triggering arbitrary code execution via the vulnerable parser. \n\nDo not use `full_load` or `FullLoader` with external input. The advisory confirms versions <5.4 are affected, and 5.4.1+ contains the fix. Strictly follow these steps to eliminate the critical risk. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-04 (s0036_rel id 20077): pyyaml affected < 5.4, severity critical. CVE-2020-14343: Arbitrary code execution when untrusted YAML is parsed with full_load or FullLoader. Fixed in 5.4."
