2026-11-05T07:22:06.772-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="d474d372-bc81-47df-ae45-9e62067cb8a4" status="approved" answer="The vulnerable version range for requests leaking the Proxy-Authorization header (CVE-2023-32681) is **>= 2.3.0 and < 2.31.0**. This vulnerability allows the header to leak during HTTPS redirects. The fix was implemented in **version 2.31.0**, not 2.13.0. The advisory (s0036_rel id 20078) explicitly states the affected range ends at 2.31.0, meaning **version 2.31.0 or higher** resolves the issue. There is no fix in 2.13.0 for this specific vulnerability; the user's plan incorrectly references 2.13.0. Users must upgrade to **requests 2.31.0+** to prevent the Proxy-Authorization leak. Always verify versions against the advisory's exact affected range to avoid confusion. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-05 (s0036_rel id 20078): requests affected >= 2.3.0, < 2.31.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-32681: Proxy-Authorization header leaked to the destination server on HTTPS redirects. Fixed in 2.31.0."
