2026-11-05T07:22:26.644-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="122ea433-29be-4d1b-bbdc-625ddf3ee244" status="approved" answer="Yes, Spring4Shell (CVE-2022-22965) is a critical vulnerability in `spring-beans` per the s0036_rel advisory (id 20079). The vulnerability affects `spring-beans` versions **>= 5.3.0** but **< 5.3.18** and allows remote code execution on JDK 9+ via data binding. Official databases confirm its severity as **critical**. This matches the vulnerability's reported scope: Spring4Shell specifically exploits `spring-beans` in this version range. The fix was released in **5.3.18**. No other packages or versions are impacted by this specific CVE. The advisory explicitly states this critical severity for the affected `spring-beans` range, with no contradictions to the provided facts. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-06 (s0036_rel id 20079): spring-beans affected >= 5.3.0, < 5.3.18, severity critical. CVE-2022-22965: Remote code execution through data binding on JDK 9+ (Spring4Shell). Fixed in 5.3.18."
