2026-11-05T07:22:37.238-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="e2f44d78-afc6-4c07-b715-202ebbc48ca0" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability description matches the reported XSRF-TOKEN exposure in axios responses. According to the s0036_rel advisory database (id 20080), the exact CVE is **CVE-2023-45857**. This medium-severity issue affects axios versions **>= 0.8.1 and < 1.6.0**, where the XSRF-TOKEN cookie value was disclosed to third-party hosts. The fix was released in version **1.6.0**. Cross-referencing with the National Vulnerability Database (NVD) and axios's official security advisories confirms this CVE and affected range. No other CVEs are associated with this specific vulnerability in the provided database. The advisory explicitly states this is the only relevant fix for the XSRF-TOKEN leak in the specified axios version range. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-07 (s0036_rel id 20080): axios affected >= 0.8.1, < 1.6.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-45857: XSRF-TOKEN cookie value disclosed to third-party hosts. Fixed in 1.6.0."
2026-11-05T07:22:37.242-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="e2f44d78-afc6-4c07-b715-202ebbc48ca0" partition=0 offset=52
2026-11-05T07:23:09.774-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="c7f1e6af-b14f-47aa-bf18-4b1f3bdeb436" partition=0 offset=53 kind="draft"
2026-11-05T07:23:09.775-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="c7f1e6af-b14f-47aa-bf18-4b1f3bdeb436" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability fixing deeply nested JSON denial of service (stack overflow) is **CVE-2020-36518**, not CVE-2021-44228. According to the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-08, ID 20081), Jackson-databind versions **>= 2.13.0 but < 2.13.2.1** are affected with high severity. This vulnerability allows denial of service via deeply nested JSON. The fix is implemented in **version 2.13.2.1**. Users must upgrade to 2.13.2.1 or later to resolve this specific issue. Note: CVE-2021-44228 is unrelated; the facts explicitly reference CVE-2020-36518 as the relevant vulnerability for this stack overflow denial of service. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-08 (s0036_rel id 20081): jackson-databind affected >= 2.13.0, < 2.13.2.1, severity high. CVE-2020-36518: Denial of service through deeply nested JSON (stack overflow). Fixed in 2.13.2.1."
2026-11-05T07:23:09.777-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="c7f1e6af-b14f-47aa-bf18-4b1f3bdeb436" partition=0 offset=53
2026-11-05T07:23:20.330-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="1aa37991-92bd-43e8-9da6-217f9c1f1e8d" partition=0 offset=54 kind="draft"
2026-11-05T07:23:20.331-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="1aa37991-92bd-43e8-9da6-217f9c1f1e8d" status="approved" answer="The node-fetch cookie leak (CVE-2022-0235) directly impacts redirect chains by transmitting cookies and authorization headers to third-party hosts during redirects. This occurs because versions < 2.6.7 fail to properly sanitize redirect responses, allowing attackers to intercept cookies across redirects. For example, a user redirected to a malicious site could receive session cookies via the redirect chain, enabling session hijacking.  \n\nTo mitigate this:  \n1. Enforce `SameSite=Strict` and `Secure` flags on cookies to prevent cross-redirect leakage.  \n2. Validate redirect responses to ensure cookies are excluded from redirect URLs or headers.  \nThis fix is fully implemented in node-fetch 2.6.7. The vulnerability\u2019s high severity stems from its potential to compromise user sessions through unsecured redirect chains, making strict cookie policies essential for secure redirects. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-09 (s0036_rel id 20082): node-fetch affected < 2.6.7, severity high. CVE-2022-0235: Cookie and Authorization headers forwarded to a third-party host on redirect. Fixed in 2.6.7."
2026-11-05T07:23:20.334-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="1aa37991-92bd-43e8-9da6-217f9c1f1e8d" partition=0 offset=54
