2026-11-05T07:23:43.757-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="718f67f5-2761-4b51-a997-28e2d687edab" status="approved" answer="The fixed version for the header-count denial of service vulnerability (CVE-2024-37890) in the `ws` package is **8.17.1**. This fix addresses the high-severity issue where requests exceeding `server.maxHeadersCount` could cause denial of service. The advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-10, s0036_rel id 20083) confirms the vulnerability affects `ws` versions >= 8.0.0 but < 8.17.1. Version 8.17.1 resolves this by properly validating header counts, preventing the denial of service. No other versions are specified as fixed in this advisory. Users should upgrade to 8.17.1 or later to mitigate the risk. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-10 (s0036_rel id 20083): ws affected >= 8.0.0, < 8.17.1, severity high. CVE-2024-37890: Denial of service from a request whose header count exceeds server.maxHeadersCount. Fixed in 8.17.1."
2026-11-05T07:23:43.758-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="718f67f5-2761-4b51-a997-28e2d687edab" partition=0 offset=55
