2026-11-05T08:03:58.936-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="1dc180ef-ed52-4f40-8769-566385178b4f" status="approved" answer="minimist versions 1.0.0 through 1.2.5.x are vulnerable to prototype pollution (critical severity). This is documented in advisory VULN-0036-HW9-03 (s0036_rel id 20076), which identifies minimist as affected for versions >= 1.0.0 and < 1.2.6. The vulnerability (CVE-2021-44906) allows attackers to pollute prototypes via crafted command-line arguments, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution. The fix was released in minimist version 1.2.6. Organizations using minimist versions prior to 1.2.6 must upgrade immediately to mitigate this critical risk. Always verify the exact affected range against the advisory to ensure timely patching. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-03 (s0036_rel id 20076): minimist affected >= 1.0.0, < 1.2.6, severity critical. CVE-2021-44906: Prototype pollution through crafted command-line arguments. Fixed in 1.2.6."
2026-11-05T08:03:58.939-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="1dc180ef-ed52-4f40-8769-566385178b4f" partition=0 offset=124
