2026-11-05T08:05:03.632-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="7247b8a4-2c05-473d-b3a7-1c500b87620a" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability fixing the Proxy-Authorization header leak (CVE-2023-32681) is addressed in requests version 2.31.0. According to the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-05, id 20078), the affected range is requests >= 2.3.0 and < 2.31.0. This medium-severity issue caused the Proxy-Authorization header to leak to destination servers during HTTPS redirects. Version 2.31.0 contains the fix. Users must upgrade to 2.31.0 or later to resolve this specific leak. Note: The query referenced CVE-2021-40344, but the facts confirm CVE-2023-32681 is the relevant vulnerability for this header leak. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-05 (s0036_rel id 20078): requests affected >= 2.3.0, < 2.31.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-32681: Proxy-Authorization header leaked to the destination server on HTTPS redirects. Fixed in 2.31.0."
2026-11-05T08:05:03.635-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="7247b8a4-2c05-473d-b3a7-1c500b87620a" partition=0 offset=126
