2026-11-05T08:06:05.623-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="9b51c3f1-3792-47a9-ad5d-d691c5c17351" status="approved" answer="The CVE ID covering the axios XSRF-TOKEN disclosure vulnerability is **CVE-2023-45857**. This medium-severity issue affects axios versions **>= 0.8.1** and **< 1.6.0**. The vulnerability allows the XSRF-TOKEN cookie value to be disclosed to third-party hosts, potentially enabling cross-site request forgery attacks. The fix was implemented in axios version **1.6.0**. This aligns with the advisory database entry VULN-0036-HW9-07 (s0036_rel id 20080), which confirms the affected range, severity, and resolution. No other CVEs are associated with this specific disclosure mechanism in the provided facts. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-07 (s0036_rel id 20080): axios affected >= 0.8.1, < 1.6.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-45857: XSRF-TOKEN cookie value disclosed to third-party hosts. Fixed in 1.6.0."
2026-11-05T08:06:05.627-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="9b51c3f1-3792-47a9-ad5d-d691c5c17351" partition=0 offset=127
