2026-11-05T08:07:07.580-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="cc7b6ab1-b4e6-4e38-957c-c3591381660d" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability patched in Jackson-databind for deeply nested JSON Denial of Service (stack overflow) is CVE-2020-36518. According to the s0036_rel advisory (ID 20081), this high-severity issue affected versions **>= 2.13.0 but < 2.13.2.1**. The fix was implemented in **version 2.13.2.1**, resolving the stack overflow vulnerability triggered by excessively nested JSON structures. This patch addresses the specific DoS vector where maliciously crafted JSON could cause excessive stack consumption. Users must upgrade to 2.13.2.1 or later to mitigate this critical vulnerability. No other versions were patched for this specific issue. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-08 (s0036_rel id 20081): jackson-databind affected >= 2.13.0, < 2.13.2.1, severity high. CVE-2020-36518: Denial of service through deeply nested JSON (stack overflow). Fixed in 2.13.2.1."
2026-11-05T08:07:07.583-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="cc7b6ab1-b4e6-4e38-957c-c3591381660d" partition=0 offset=128
2026-11-05T08:07:18.602-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="1a4948d1-0417-41d7-ad73-86b2bb65e1e8" partition=0 offset=129 kind="draft"
2026-11-05T08:07:18.603-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="1a4948d1-0417-41d7-ad73-86b2bb65e1e8" status="approved" answer="An attacker exploiting the node-fetch redirect cookie leak (CVE-2022-0235) can steal victim session cookies during redirect responses to third-party hosts. This occurs because versions of node-fetch before 2.6.7 improperly forward cookies and authorization headers in redirect requests. Once stolen, attackers hijack user sessions by using these cookies to impersonate victims. Consequently, they can perform unauthorized actions on behalf of the victim, such as accessing sensitive data, modifying accounts, or executing malicious operations without valid authentication. The vulnerability (VULN-0036-HW9-09) has high severity and is fixed in node-fetch 2.6.7. Organizations using affected versions must upgrade immediately to prevent session hijacking via redirect leaks. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-09 (s0036_rel id 20082): node-fetch affected < 2.6.7, severity high. CVE-2022-0235: Cookie and Authorization headers forwarded to a third-party host on redirect. Fixed in 2.6.7."
2026-11-05T08:07:18.608-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="1a4948d1-0417-41d7-ad73-86b2bb65e1e8" partition=0 offset=129
