2026-11-05T08:08:13.084-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="23c5027d-3866-41df-b0f9-92a98bb69626" status="approved" answer="The `ws` package vulnerability CVE-2024-37890 (high severity) allows denial of service via requests exceeding `server.maxHeadersCount`. This affects versions **>= 8.0.0 and < 8.17.1**. The patch is specifically included in **version 8.17.1**, which resolves the issue by addressing the header count handling mechanism. This fix ensures the server can safely process requests without crashing due to excessive headers. Users should update to 8.17.1 or later to mitigate this vulnerability. The advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-10, id 20083) confirms this version range and fix. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-10 (s0036_rel id 20083): ws affected >= 8.0.0, < 8.17.1, severity high. CVE-2024-37890: Denial of service from a request whose header count exceeds server.maxHeadersCount. Fixed in 8.17.1."
