2026-11-05T08:08:25.234-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="9c4a920a-f536-4b5c-ae61-f3a18304c61c" status="approved" answer="The CVE for the Log4Shell vulnerability in log4j-core is **CVE-2021-44228**. This critical vulnerability (severity: critical) affects log4j-core versions **>= 2.0-beta9** and **< 2.15.0**. It enables remote code execution through JNDI lookups in logged strings, allowing attackers to execute arbitrary code on vulnerable systems. CVE-2021-44228 is the primary Log4Shell vulnerability identified in the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-01, id 20074). The fix was released in log4j-core 2.15.0, which resolved the remote code execution risk by mitigating the JNDI lookup exploit. This vulnerability represents the most severe Log4Shell impact on the log4j-core component, directly affecting systems using older versions before patching. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-01 (s0036_rel id 20074): log4j-core affected >= 2.0-beta9, < 2.15.0, severity critical. CVE-2021-44228: Remote code execution through JNDI lookups in logged strings (Log4Shell). Fixed in 2.15.0."
