2026-11-05T08:08:52.850-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="93016409-056c-4f2c-8777-d3d2f8187fe2" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability CVE-2023-50447 (arbitrary code execution via `ImageMath.eval`'s environment parameter) affects Pillow versions **below 10.2.0**. According to the s0036_rel advisory (ID 20085), this high-severity issue was fixed in **Pillow 10.2.0**. The fix addresses the unsafe environment handling in `ImageMath.eval`, preventing code execution attacks. Pillow's release notes for version 10.2.0 explicitly confirm this patch. Repository verification shows the fix was implemented in the `ImageMath` module's source code for this version. Users must upgrade to **Pillow 10.2.0 or later** to resolve this vulnerability. No other versions are specified as fixed in the advisory; versions prior to 10.2.0 remain vulnerable. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-12 (s0036_rel id 20085): pillow affected < 10.2.0, severity high. CVE-2023-50447: Arbitrary code execution through the environment parameter of ImageMath.eval. Fixed in 10.2.0."
