2026-11-05T08:09:47.759-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="09102c06-3e89-4bb8-b494-d21ec4916d49" status="approved" answer="The affected versions of protobufjs for the prototype pollution vulnerability (CVE-2023-36665) are **7.0.0 to 7.2.3 inclusive**. This critical severity vulnerability (VULN-0036-HW9-16, s0036_rel id 20089) allows prototype pollution via crafted protobuf definitions. The fix was released in version 7.2.4. Therefore, all versions from 7.0.0 up to but excluding 7.2.4 are vulnerable. Organizations should upgrade to 7.2.4 or later to resolve this risk. The advisory explicitly states affected versions as >=7.0.0 and <7.2.4, confirming the range. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-16 (s0036_rel id 20089): protobufjs affected >= 7.0.0, < 7.2.4, severity critical. CVE-2023-36665: Prototype pollution through crafted protobuf definitions. Fixed in 7.2.4."
