2026-11-05T08:10:46.670-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="31323b4d-a000-400f-8129-475cb54758ee" status="approved" answer="The vulnerability CVE-2023-32681 (Proxy-Authorization header leak during HTTPS redirects) was first introduced in requests version 2.3.0. This is confirmed by the s0036_rel advisory database (id 20078), which states the affected range is requests >= 2.3.0 and < 2.31.0. The vulnerability was fixed in version 2.31.0. The advisory specifies medium severity for this issue. No earlier versions of requests contained this vulnerability, as the affected range begins at 2.3.0. This aligns with the exact facts provided in the advisory database. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-05 (s0036_rel id 20078): requests affected >= 2.3.0, < 2.31.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-32681: Proxy-Authorization header leaked to the destination server on HTTPS redirects. Fixed in 2.31.0."
