2026-11-05T08:11:10.769-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="c6ab0c1a-58cf-4642-ac49-19cb0c09bf17" status="approved" answer="No, the Spring4Shell vulnerability (CVE-2022-22965) is **not exploitable** in Spring Framework 5.3.18. The advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-06, id 20079) explicitly states that spring-beans is affected for versions **>= 5.3.0 but < 5.3.18**. Since 5.3.18 includes the critical patch for this vulnerability (Remote Code Execution on JDK 9+), it is fully mitigated in this specific framework release. The vulnerability was resolved in 5.3.18 through the Spring Framework update, making exploitation impossible in this version. Always verify the *framework* version (not individual modules) when assessing vulnerability status, as the advisory tracks the entire Spring Framework release line. For Spring4Shell, 5.3.18 is the first secure version in the 5.3.x series. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-06 (s0036_rel id 20079): spring-beans affected >= 5.3.0, < 5.3.18, severity critical. CVE-2022-22965: Remote code execution through data binding on JDK 9+ (Spring4Shell). Fixed in 5.3.18."
