2026-11-05T08:11:25.732-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="006e6cc2-24ba-446e-8b1b-6992cfcd449d" status="approved" answer="The CVE for the Express open redirect vulnerability is **CVE-2024-29041**. This vulnerability affects Express.js versions **< 4.19.2** and has a **medium severity** rating. It allows attackers to exploit open redirects via malformed URLs passed to `res.location` and `res.redirect`. The fix was released in Express.js **4.19.2**. This aligns with the advisory database entry VULN-0036-HW9-11 (s0036_rel id 20084), which specifically identifies this issue as an open redirect vulnerability in Express. No other CVEs or versions are associated with this specific vulnerability in the provided facts. The advisory confirms the affected range, severity, and resolution without additional context. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-11 (s0036_rel id 20084): express affected < 4.19.2, severity medium. CVE-2024-29041: Open redirect through malformed URLs passed to res.location and res.redirect. Fixed in 4.19.2."
